Akaunting is installed under /srv/www/akaunting. The web server
document root is that directory, not public/. Configuration is
/etc/sysconfig/akaunting, symlinked to /srv/www/akaunting/.env.

Akaunting 3.2.4 is Business Source License 1.1. Production use is
limited to one company, two users, and one thousand invoices, and it
may not be offered as an accounting service to third parties. Four
years after publication the same code becomes GPLv3.

1. Create a MariaDB database:

   mariadb -e "CREATE DATABASE akaunting CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;"
   mariadb -e "CREATE USER akaunting@localhost IDENTIFIED BY 'a-password';"
   mariadb -e "GRANT ALL ON akaunting.* TO akaunting@localhost;"
   systemctl enable --now mariadb

2. Put the same password and a real APP_URL into /etc/sysconfig/akaunting.

3. Enable the site:

   ln -s ../sites-available/akaunting.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/akaunting.conf
   systemctl enable --now php-fpm@akaunting nginx akaunting-scheduler.timer

4. Open the site. The installer creates the company and the admin user.
   Leave APP_INSTALLED=false until that wizard finishes.
